.TH GIGACTLD 8 "2026-07-25" "gigactl 1.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
gigactld \- GigaControl daemon for Gigabyte G5/G6 fan and keyboard control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gigactld
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.br
.B gigactld \-\-restore-firmware
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gigactld
is the root service that owns Embedded Controller access on Gigabyte G5/G6
laptops and exposes it on the D\-Bus system bus. It is the single writer of the
controller: the desktop app and the
.BR gfan (1)
and
.BR gkbd (1)
command line tools are unprivileged clients of it, which is what keeps two
processes from interleaving controller command sequences.
.PP
On each poll it publishes a
.B Telemetry
signal \(em CPU and GPU temperature, both fans' RPM and duty cycle \(em and runs
the active fan profile, applying whatever duty cycle the curve calls for at the
current temperature. It also remembers the fan profile, the custom curves and the
keyboard colour and brightness, re\-applying them at boot and after resume from
suspend.
.PP
Every write is authorised through polkit before it happens, using the caller's
bus name as the subject. The shipped policy allows the user of the active local
session to control the fans and backlight without a password, and requires
administrator authentication otherwise \(em which means a remote session such as
SSH has no polkit agent to satisfy, and should run its client as root instead.
.PP
The service is normally managed by systemd and not run by hand:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl status gigactl.service
.EE
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fIseconds\fR
How often to read the controller, publish telemetry and apply the fan curve.
Defaults to 2 seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-restore-firmware
Hand both fans back to the laptop firmware's own curve and exit immediately. The
unit runs this after the main process stops, including after a crash, so the fans
can never be left frozen at a stale manual duty cycle.
.SH EMBEDDED CONTROLLER ACCESS
Two backends, chosen at startup. Preferred is the
.B ec_sys
debugfs interface, where the kernel's own driver performs and serialises each
transaction. The fallback is raw port I/O through
.IR /dev/port ,
which races the kernel driver and is used only when the module is unavailable.
.PP
The package therefore loads
.B ec_sys
with write support at boot, and the unit runs
.B modprobe
before starting, so the preferred backend is present even on the first start
after installation. Which one is in use is logged at startup.
.SH D-BUS INTERFACE
.B gigactld
owns
.B io.github.smairio.gigactl
on the system bus, at
.I /io/github/smairio/gigactl
with interface
.BR io.github.smairio.gigactl.Control .
Methods:
.BR SetFanDuty ,
.BR RestoreFirmware ,
.BR SetProfile ,
.BR SetCurve ,
.BR SetKeyboardColor ,
.B SetKeyboardBrightness
and
.BR SetKeyboardEnabled .
Properties:
.BR DaemonVersion ,
.BR ActiveProfile ,
.BR Telemetry ,
.B KeyboardState
and
.BR Curves .
Reading is unrestricted; every method is gated by polkit.
.PP
.RS
.EX
busctl introspect io.github.smairio.gigactl /io/github/smairio/gigactl
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/gigactl/state.json
The saved fan profile, custom curves and keyboard state, restored at startup.
Removed when the package is purged.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/gigactl.service
The unit. Enabled and started when the package is installed.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/io.github.smairio.gigactl.conf
Bus policy: only root may own the name; any user may call the interface, and
polkit decides inside the daemon.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.smairio.gigactl.policy
The
.B control-fans
and
.B control-keyboard
actions and their defaults.
.TP
.I /run/lock/gigactl-ec.lock
Held for the duration of each controller transaction, and taken by
.BR gfan (1)
and
.BR gkbd (1)
when they write the controller directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 1 if the Embedded Controller cannot be opened, and 0 on a clean shutdown or
after
.BR \-\-restore-firmware .
.SH NOTES
If the daemon is stopped, the fans return to firmware control rather than
staying where it left them. Recovering by hand, should it ever be needed:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo gigactld \-\-restore-firmware
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gigactl-gui (1),
.BR gfan (1),
.BR gkbd (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
The reverse\-engineered controller protocol is documented in
.I /usr/share/doc/gigactl
and at
.UR https://github.com/smairio/gigactl
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
khalil Smairi
